    {
      "id": "7pv1de2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Constitutional Articles Related to President"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The President is the head of the Indian State, first citizen of India, and supreme commander of the defence forces.",
        "Elected by an Electoral College comprising elected members of Parliament and elected members of Legislative Assemblies of States and UTs (Delhi, Puducherry, J&K).",
        "Under Article 61, the President can be impeached only on the ground of 'violation of the Constitution'.",
        "Article 123 empowers the President to promulgate ordinances during recess of Parliament, which must be approved within 6 weeks of reassembly.",
        "Pardoning power under Article 72 extends to court-martial sentences, offenses against Union law, and all cases of death sentences."
      ],
      "id": "5p81i4z"
    },
