        ]
      ],
      "id": "vd148ho"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xhuep2g",
      "content": "• No money bill can be introduced without President's recommendation"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "c8juj8v",
      "content": "• President causes the Union Budget to be presented in Parliament"
    },
    {
      "id": "891aw06",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Judicial Powers"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "60fat68",
      "content": "• Can grant pardon, reprieve, respite, remission and commutation of punishment under Article 72"
    },
    {
      "id": "w7f5r0m",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Emergency Powers"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "w6txxii",
      "content": "• National Emergency (Article 352)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hkotin5",
      "content": "• President's Rule in states (Article 356)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "k9pjudp",
      "content": "• Financial Emergency (Article 360)"
    },
    {
      "id": "04g2a7o",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Impeachment of the President"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rgt6u69",
      "content": "• The President can be removed for violation of the Constitution."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0b4km65",
      "content": "• The impeachment process can be initiated in either House of Parliament."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Nominated members of Parliament DO NOT participate in the election of the President, but THEY DO participate in the impeachment process.",
        "Elected members of State Legislative Assemblies participate in the presidential election, but DO NOT participate in the impeachment process.",
        "The ground for impeachment—'violation of the Constitution'—is mentioned in Article 61 but is NOT defined anywhere in the Constitution.",
        "An ordinance issued by the President under Article 123 has a maximum spatial life of 6 months and 6 weeks without parliamentary approval."
      ],
      "id": "esbyz3n"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5fdx6lv",
      "content": "• A two-thirds majority is required."
    },
    {
      "id": "760sdii",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "EXAM Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sct449f",
      "content": "• First President of India – Dr. Rajendra Prasad"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "8q707yt",
      "content": "• President is elected indirectly"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z70y24p",
      "content": "• Term of President – 5 years"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f7cf78v",
      "content": "• Oath administered by Chief Justice of India"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t1hsp4w",
      "content": "• Article 72 deals with pardoning power"
    }
  ],
